course: dictionary
lesson: 14406
title: Overcook: too much of a good thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «overcook» has the prefix over-, which means too much. To overcook food is to cook it for too long. «Mum forgot the timer, so the pasta was overcooked and mushy.» The clues are forgot the timer and mushy: the pasta had too much heat for too long.
explain: Overcook also has a second, informal meaning. «He overcooked the ending of his story, with dragons, storms and three fights on one page.» Here nobody put the story in a pan. It means he went too far and made the ending much too dramatic.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about food, the meaning is cooked for too long. If it is about a story, a game or a feeling, the meaning is to do something too much. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Overcook is a verb: overcook, overcooks, overcooked, overcooking.
fact: «Overcooked» means cooked for too long, so the food is dry, hard, burnt or mushy.
fact: «Overcooked vegetables» are often soft and mushy, and «overcook the pasta» means you cooked it for too long.
fact: Informal: «overcook» can mean to overdo something, like telling a story with too much drama.
fact: The prefix over- often means too much, as in overfill, overeat and overwork.
exercise: «Mum forgot the timer, so the pasta was overcooked and mushy.» What does overcooked mean here? | Cooked with too much salt | Cooked very quickly | Not cooked at all | *Cooked for too long, so it is mushy
exercise: «The toast was overcooked and black.» What had happened to the toast? | It had been served cold | It had been eaten by the dog | It had been cut into fingers | *It had been left in the heat too long
exercise: «He overcooked the ending of his story, with dragons and three fights.» What does overcooked mean in this sentence? | He wrote the ending in a frying pan | *He made the ending much too dramatic | He finished the story very quickly | He left the ending out
test: «Please do not overcook the peas, or they will go soft.» What should you avoid? | Cooking them with butter | Eating them cold | Buying them frozen | *Cooking them for too long
test: «Ella overcooks every joke until nobody laughs.» What does overcooks mean? | *Does something too much, until it stops working | Forgets a joke | Tells a joke very quietly | Cooks something at a very low heat
exam: «The pasta was overcooked, so Dad made a new batch.» What does the word overcooked tell you? | The pasta was cooked in a new pan | The pasta was cooked too quickly and is raw | The pasta was not cooked at all | *The pasta was cooked for too long and spoilt
